   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "A neat example is the gastroileal reflex. Food stretches the stomach. Impulses travel through the myenteric plexus, mediated by the vagus, and a fast peristaltic wave runs down to the ilium. The ileocecal valve relaxes, helped by gastrin and CCK, and chyme passes into the cecum. A new meal makes room for itself."
  }
 ],
